{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773182816,"nonce":"VrF0zDJ5imp8EoVNO4pwd3CT03A=","title":"\"Branch merged — safe to dismiss\" pill is redundant on completed auth requests","message":"Completed auth requests show a green \"Branch merged — safe to dismiss\" pill. This is always true for completed requests (auth-merge deletes the branch as part of the merge), so the pill is redundant noise.\n\nThe `isBranchMerged()` check in `ui/src/views/auth.tsx` verifies the branch ref no longer exists — but that condition is *always* met for completed requests. The pill should be removed from the history view for completed items.\n\nFix: remove the `{branchMerged \u0026\u0026 \u003cspan className=\"branch-merged-tag\"\u003e...}` block (around line 527) from the auth history item render.","files":null}]}